1
00:01:38,070 --> 00:01:43,920
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:46,890
[Episode 8]

3
00:01:46,979 --> 00:01:49,570
[Emergency]

4
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:03,590
Doctor,

5
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:06,000
Between emergency
and regular registration,

6
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,000
which one is cheaper?

7
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,080
They're the same.

8
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:08,910
Just go over there.

9
00:02:08,910 --> 00:02:10,630
Register over there. Over there.

10
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:11,750
I don't really have a serious problem.

11
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:12,840
I just dropped something on my foot

12
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:13,810
while working a couple of days ago.

13
00:02:13,810 --> 00:02:14,710
Go ahead.

14
00:02:14,710 --> 00:02:16,170
Just register over there.

15
00:02:17,910 --> 00:02:19,240
Sit here. Let me take a look.

16
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,300
Thank you, Doctor.

17
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:22,810
It just got smashed.

18
00:02:25,630 --> 00:02:26,690
Take off your sock.

19
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,680
How many days has it been?

20
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:31,079
It happened last Saturday.

21
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,070
[Wishing You a Speedy Recovery]

22
00:02:31,079 --> 00:02:32,840
I-It's been about 5 or 6 days.

23
00:02:32,579 --> 00:02:36,910
[Wishing You a Speedy Recovery]

24
00:02:34,030 --> 00:02:35,240
It might hurt a bit.

25
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:35,970
Bear with it.

26
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:41,180
The proximal joint

27
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:42,750
of the second toe on your right foot

28
00:02:42,750 --> 00:02:44,400
is swollen and deformed.

29
00:02:45,630 --> 00:02:47,150
It looks like a localized fracture.

30
00:02:47,150 --> 00:02:54,970
[No smoking]

31
00:02:47,470 --> 00:02:48,470
You need to have

32
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:50,380
reduction and fixation surgery.

33
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:52,560
Go to the orthopedics department
over there

34
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,520
and register.

35
00:02:54,190 --> 00:02:55,800
Over... over there.

36
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:56,960
Go. Go register.

37
00:02:58,630 --> 00:02:59,280
Doctor.

38
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:01,870
I don't have money for surgery.

39
00:03:01,870 --> 00:03:03,080
I can put up with the pain.

40
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:04,960
Could you prescribe
some painkillers for me?

41
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,490
You have to register first.

42
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,240
If you don't register,

43
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:08,400
you can't get the medicine.

44
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,530
Lie down in the back.

45
00:03:09,590 --> 00:03:10,250
Over there.

46
00:03:10,310 --> 00:03:11,400
Thank you, Doctor.

47
00:03:11,590 --> 00:03:12,190
Thank you.

48
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:16,020
Be careful.

49
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:19,910
Sorry for the trouble.

50
00:03:19,910 --> 00:03:22,240
No need to take off your shoes.
Just lie down.

51
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:22,900
Don't move.

52
00:03:37,579 --> 00:03:40,500
[Emergency Surgery Department]

53
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:11,440
Alright, we're done.

54
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:13,000
Thank you, Doctor.

55
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:17,360
[No smoking]

56
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:15,650
Sit there and wait a moment.

57
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:31,070
Here, these two medicines
are for inflammation and pain relief.

58
00:04:31,070 --> 00:04:32,400
They're not expensive.

59
00:04:32,510 --> 00:04:33,360
Most pharmacies

60
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:34,240
sell them.

61
00:04:34,830 --> 00:04:35,830
Buy 1 box of the one on top

62
00:04:35,830 --> 00:04:37,000
and 3 boxes of the one on the bottom.

63
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Take them according to the instructions.

64
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:38,750
Okay.

65
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:40,070
Thank you, Doctor.

66
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,270
It's nothing. Go ahead.

67
00:04:41,270 --> 00:04:41,950
Thank you.

68
00:04:42,270 --> 00:04:43,240
Thank you.

69
00:04:48,750 --> 00:04:51,010
Don't let the president know about this.

70
00:04:52,310 --> 00:04:53,000
About what?

71
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:54,830
Nothing.

72
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,310
Shall we go to the hospital entrance
at noon

73
00:04:58,310 --> 00:04:58,830
to grab a bite?

74
00:04:58,830 --> 00:04:59,630
My treat.

75
00:04:59,830 --> 00:05:01,490
I have something to do at noon.

76
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:02,750
What is it?

77
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:13,720
He definitely wouldn't have

78
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:15,970
broken the rules like this before.

79
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:17,870
And then?

80
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:19,420
Didn't you remind him?

81
00:05:19,750 --> 00:05:20,720
I did.

82
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:22,720
Then I changed the subject.

83
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:23,430
I said,

84
00:05:23,430 --> 00:05:24,890
"I'll treat you to lunch."

85
00:05:40,159 --> 00:05:40,720
Oh no.

86
00:05:41,630 --> 00:05:43,560
He comes and goes as he pleases now.

87
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:48,480
How about

88
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:49,980
we go to the president?

89
00:05:56,830 --> 00:05:58,750
We're out of options.

90
00:05:59,070 --> 00:06:00,600
President, you are wise.

91
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:01,360
You have many ideas.

92
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,490
Think of something.

93
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:06,040
Every lock has its key.

94
00:06:06,870 --> 00:06:08,160
He has the key.

95
00:06:09,070 --> 00:06:10,750
If he doesn't want to open it,
there's nothing anyone can do.

96
00:06:10,750 --> 00:06:11,600
Then what should we do?

97
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:13,040
Are we just going to leave him alone?

98
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:13,950
The thing is, this guy...

99
00:06:13,950 --> 00:06:15,120
He's a really nice guy.

100
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,070
If things keep going like this,

101
00:06:16,070 --> 00:06:17,000
I'm afraid he won't be able to hold on.

102
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,400
Then he can just lie down.

103
00:06:19,310 --> 00:06:19,870
Huang,

104
00:06:19,870 --> 00:06:21,480
others might not understand this logic,

105
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:22,560
but how could you not?

106
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,830
Well, it's fine if I lie down.

107
00:06:24,830 --> 00:06:25,920
I'd be quite comfortable lying down.

108
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:27,390
But... he can't.

109
00:06:27,390 --> 00:06:28,800
H-He just can't lie down.

110
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:30,180
Then what should we do?

111
00:06:31,310 --> 00:06:33,170
Think of a way to make him lie down?

112
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:34,680
Can you think of one?

113
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:35,510
How could I?

114
00:06:35,510 --> 00:06:36,750
I can't...

115
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:37,240
I can't think of anything.

116
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:38,430
Can you?

117
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:42,370
Then what are you two worrying about here?

118
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:46,380
Lie down if you need to.

119
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:48,140
And stand up if you need to.

120
00:06:48,390 --> 00:06:49,390
I'll just eat when I need to.

121
00:06:49,390 --> 00:06:50,590
Do you guys want some?

122
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:11,680
She was crying

123
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,530
when she got discharged
early in the morning.

124
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:26,250
[Ai Chen]

125
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:24,070
Pick a photo of Aunt Ling

126
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:26,560
and send it to me before tomorrow night.

127
00:09:34,850 --> 00:09:38,760
[Remembered for All Time]

128
00:09:45,270 --> 00:09:46,320
Look.

129
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:48,320
I know it's not easy for you,

130
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:49,450
a widow with a child.

131
00:09:50,150 --> 00:09:51,120
This package...

132
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:54,170
including transportation,
ceremony, storage,

133
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,120
urn,

134
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,440
burial, funeral,

135
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:58,840
wreaths, and condolence couplets,

136
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:00,240
is only 150 yuan in total.

137
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,600
I'm really not making any money off this.

138
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:03,000
It's not about the money.

139
00:10:03,150 --> 00:10:04,870
As long as he can be cremated and buried,
that's fine.

140
00:10:04,870 --> 00:10:06,530
Keep everything else simple.

141
00:10:06,670 --> 00:10:07,480
Ling.

142
00:10:07,750 --> 00:10:09,080
Don't keep it simple.

143
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,080
I'll pay for it.

144
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:13,080
We've discussed it,

145
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,880
and we're willing to cover half.

146
00:10:16,630 --> 00:10:17,890
I don't need your help.

147
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,240
I said it's not about the money.

148
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,120
The most important thing for me right now

149
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:22,870
is to give birth

150
00:10:22,870 --> 00:10:24,070
to this child safely.

151
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:29,480
When Liu was alive,

152
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:30,670
we discussed it.

153
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,400
No matter who dies first,

154
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:35,690
we won't have a funeral.

155
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:39,030
Having each other in our hearts
is better than anything.

156
00:10:39,030 --> 00:10:40,390
I'm Liu's wife.

157
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:41,630
I have the final say.

158
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:45,480
There will be no funeral.

159
00:11:21,630 --> 00:11:22,840
You never surprise me

160
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:24,240
but always scare me, huh?

161
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:28,180
But it's good that you moved back.

162
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:34,000
You look fine to me,

163
00:11:36,510 --> 00:11:38,200
but you're not really fine.

164
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,900
You need to eat and sleep well.

165
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,320
You've been bottling up too many emotions.

166
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:45,380
You have to find a way to release them.

167
00:11:45,390 --> 00:11:47,390
Although it's hard to think of a way,

168
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:49,030
I'm sure you can figure it out.

169
00:11:49,030 --> 00:11:51,560
Otherwise,
you'll hurt yourself and others.

170
00:12:05,270 --> 00:12:06,270
We don't need him.

171
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:08,660
He doesn't need to attend.

172
00:12:08,750 --> 00:12:09,750
Why are you going?

173
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:11,780
What's the point of you going?

174
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,120
Up until now,

175
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:14,720
he hasn't shed a single tear.

176
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:15,510
In his heart,

177
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:16,510
he's cold-blooded

178
00:12:16,510 --> 00:12:17,440
to the bone!

179
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:19,100
Cold-blooded!

180
00:12:35,870 --> 00:12:36,750
I thought about quitting.

181
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:37,550
I couldn't play anymore.

182
00:12:37,550 --> 00:12:38,550
In the last round,

183
00:12:38,630 --> 00:12:39,510
I was waiting for a Baozhongbao.

184
00:12:39,510 --> 00:12:40,440
Darn it!

185
00:12:42,630 --> 00:12:43,490
What happened?

186
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,360
And then?

187
00:12:47,390 --> 00:12:49,080
I was so excited.

188
00:12:49,150 --> 00:12:50,440
If I won with a Baozhongbao,

189
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,720
wouldn't I win back everything

190
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:53,270
I lost that night?

191
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:54,600
I thought to myself at the time,

192
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:57,360
even if someone else discarded
the tile I needed, I wouldn't take it.

193
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:58,560
I wanted to draw it myself.

194
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:03,320
[Liu Zhengliang]

195
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:00,030
It means a bigger win, right?

196
00:13:00,030 --> 00:13:00,750
So I kept drawing.

197
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:02,120
One tile

198
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:02,670
after another.

199
00:13:02,670 --> 00:13:04,240
I was thinking,
if there were only 4 tiles left,

200
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:05,790
wouldn't the game be a draw?

201
00:13:05,790 --> 00:13:06,510
Right.

202
00:13:06,550 --> 00:13:08,320
Then all the time
I spent forging Baozhongbao

203
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:09,600
would... be for nothing.

204
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,320
Right.

205
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:12,290
There was just one left, so I was...

206
00:13:20,750 --> 00:13:21,480
He...

207
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:39,770
Hello everyone.

208
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:40,770
I'm Chen Junnan,

209
00:13:40,790 --> 00:13:42,650
transferred from No. 1 Hospital.

210
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:44,360
From now on, I'll be

211
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:45,560
working with you all.

212
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:46,600
Welcome.

213
00:13:47,030 --> 00:13:49,290
I brought some small gifts for everyone.

214
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:51,360
Bro.

215
00:13:51,790 --> 00:13:52,440
Bro.

216
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:53,510
Don't stand on the ceremony.

217
00:13:53,510 --> 00:13:54,770
Open it and take a look.

218
00:13:58,150 --> 00:13:59,120
Is it wild?

219
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:00,550
Yes, purely wild.

220
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,510
This stuff is hard to get.

221
00:14:07,510 --> 00:14:08,360
It's not easy to find.

222
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:09,270
Bro,

223
00:14:09,270 --> 00:14:10,510
you are too generous.

224
00:14:14,630 --> 00:14:15,440
Studying?

225
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:19,880
It's for you.

226
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:24,030
It's full of study materials
by famous teachers.

227
00:14:24,630 --> 00:14:25,830
I bought them online.

228
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:26,550
Thank you.

229
00:14:26,670 --> 00:14:27,600
You're welcome.

230
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:31,730
If you don't like it,

231
00:14:32,270 --> 00:14:34,070
that's fine. Drink some of this.

232
00:14:36,510 --> 00:14:38,000
It promotes digestion

233
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:39,440
and boosts immunity.

234
00:14:39,750 --> 00:14:42,150
When you're tired of studying, drink this.

235
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,270
Collagen.

236
00:14:43,270 --> 00:14:44,240
Okay, just put them here.

237
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:44,870
Thank you.

238
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,200
Come here, bro.

239
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:49,750
Come and sit.

240
00:14:49,750 --> 00:14:50,200
Bro.

241
00:14:51,150 --> 00:14:51,910
After work,

242
00:14:51,910 --> 00:14:52,910
if you have time,

243
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:54,700
we can have a little drink.

244
00:14:55,270 --> 00:14:56,080
You can drink?

245
00:14:56,550 --> 00:14:57,600
My tolerance is low.

246
00:14:57,600 --> 00:14:58,840
I just like having a drink.

247
00:14:58,840 --> 00:14:59,750
Okay. Alright.

248
00:14:59,750 --> 00:15:00,840
Okay.

249
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:02,340
Is this your recliner?

250
00:15:02,670 --> 00:15:03,360
Yes.

251
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,270
Can I try it?

252
00:15:04,270 --> 00:15:05,150
Go ahead.

253
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:10,280
Careful. Don't fall.

254
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:11,840
Bro, come.

255
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:12,670
I'll show you...

256
00:15:12,670 --> 00:15:13,870
I'll show you around.

257
00:15:14,270 --> 00:15:15,790
Come on, let's go.

258
00:15:18,030 --> 00:15:18,840
Mingming,

259
00:15:18,910 --> 00:15:20,310
keep an eye on my lingzhi.

260
00:15:22,150 --> 00:15:23,000
Open it and take a look.

261
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:23,510
Okay.

262
00:15:24,550 --> 00:15:25,870
Our hospital is just a bit small.

263
00:15:25,870 --> 00:15:27,120
Everything else is pretty much the same

264
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:27,960
as your No. 1 Hospital.

265
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:28,360
Yes.

266
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:28,720
Look.

267
00:15:29,030 --> 00:15:30,840
Ultrasound room, wound dressing room.

268
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:32,770
This is the medical staff passage.

269
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:33,790
Zhengliang!

270
00:15:34,550 --> 00:15:35,550
I'm here!

271
00:15:38,790 --> 00:15:39,920
What does that mean?

272
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:41,500
It means what it means.

273
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:43,580
I don't know what it means either.

274
00:16:02,790 --> 00:16:04,650
When you were in a bad mood as a kid,

275
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:07,080
we always went to the shop
by the old tower to buy candy.

276
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:08,270
Ma'am, I want this.

277
00:16:08,510 --> 00:16:10,910
-Okay. I'll get it for you.
-I'll take this.

278
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:14,400
Twenty cents.

279
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:19,670
Here.

280
00:16:19,670 --> 00:16:20,960
Okay, exact change.

281
00:16:26,030 --> 00:16:26,840
Let's go.

282
00:16:33,510 --> 00:16:35,640
I remember back in elementary school,

283
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:37,600
Aunt Ling was planning

284
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:39,000
to send you to Guangzhou.

285
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:42,040
You were unhappy for a long time,

286
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:43,960
sulking and not speaking.

287
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,510
Do you remember

288
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:50,640
what your first words were after that?

289
00:16:58,320 --> 00:17:01,120
You don't have to say anything
if you don't want to.

290
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:21,810
Actually, I feel terrible inside.

291
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:26,980
But I don't know what's wrong with me.

292
00:17:28,069 --> 00:17:30,110
Why can't I just cry?

293
00:17:37,110 --> 00:17:38,200
I heard that

294
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:40,450
when people are extremely sad,

295
00:17:42,830 --> 00:17:44,270
they just can't cry.

296
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:46,680
Wanting to cry but being unable to—

297
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:48,410
that's probably what it means.

298
00:17:51,270 --> 00:17:52,270
Actually, my mom didn't hold a funeral

299
00:17:52,270 --> 00:17:53,960
for my dad back then.

300
00:17:56,110 --> 00:17:57,200
And I never saw her

301
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,680
shed a single tear.

302
00:18:01,790 --> 00:18:03,200
And she always told me...

303
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:05,920
that...

304
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:08,860
keeping someone in your heart

305
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,320
is better than anything.

306
00:18:16,030 --> 00:18:17,350
When Aunt Ling cried,

307
00:18:17,350 --> 00:18:18,640
you just didn't see it.

308
00:18:30,550 --> 00:18:31,550
Do you have any way

309
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:32,960
to make me cry?

310
00:18:33,510 --> 00:18:35,750
Tear glands and sweat glands
are exocrine glands.

311
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:37,000
You know this, right?

312
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:39,110
Letting tears turn into sweat

313
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:40,790
and flow out is also good.

314
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:06,440
Dr. Liu,

315
00:19:06,830 --> 00:19:07,790
take a break

316
00:19:07,790 --> 00:19:08,920
and have some water.

317
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:14,830
Can you stop

318
00:19:14,830 --> 00:19:16,430
and listen to me for a second?

319
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:20,000
How about...

320
00:19:20,070 --> 00:19:20,750
you go home early tonight

321
00:19:20,750 --> 00:19:22,070
and get some sleep?

322
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:23,960
There's no rush for the PhD exam.

323
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:27,720
I knew it all along.

324
00:19:28,790 --> 00:19:29,790
Knew what?

325
00:19:30,510 --> 00:19:31,310
You don't really

326
00:19:31,310 --> 00:19:32,710
want to take the PhD exam.

327
00:19:34,790 --> 00:19:35,590
What?

328
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:38,720
I said,

329
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:41,790
you're not putting your heart
into it at all.

330
00:19:41,790 --> 00:19:44,650
You are sleepy during the day
and slack off at night.

331
00:19:44,750 --> 00:19:46,110
But I can understand.

332
00:19:46,550 --> 00:19:48,510
Staying in a place like this for too long,

333
00:19:48,510 --> 00:19:49,510
you naturally

334
00:19:49,550 --> 00:19:50,960
get lazier.

335
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:52,350
I saw that you

336
00:19:52,350 --> 00:19:54,110
haven't rested well these two days.

337
00:19:54,110 --> 00:19:54,790
So I figured I'd let you

338
00:19:54,790 --> 00:19:55,830
go home early to rest.

339
00:19:55,830 --> 00:19:57,160
What are you talking about?

340
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:58,550
I'm telling the truth.

341
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:05,750
Do you really have to

342
00:20:05,750 --> 00:20:07,010
look down on everyone?

343
00:20:07,070 --> 00:20:08,730
even when they treat you well?

344
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:11,200
What's wrong with them?

345
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,200
That's why I don't want to lie to you.

346
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:13,400
Aren't they arguing?

347
00:20:15,590 --> 00:20:16,880
Why are you so nosy?

348
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:18,440
-I just want to take a look.
-Let's go.

349
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:19,510
In your current state,

350
00:20:19,510 --> 00:20:21,790
staying in a place like this,

351
00:20:22,350 --> 00:20:23,680
you won't pass the exam.

352
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:24,270
Yes.

353
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:26,480
I fell into the mud.

354
00:20:26,550 --> 00:20:28,150
Am I not allowed to climb out?

355
00:20:28,790 --> 00:20:30,240
Besides, no matter how bad
Xiaoximen Hospital is,

356
00:20:30,240 --> 00:20:30,920
is it up to a fired doctor

357
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:32,650
like you to pass judgment on it?

358
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:51,790
Let me tell you,

359
00:20:51,790 --> 00:20:53,270
don't be so nosy all day.

360
00:20:53,270 --> 00:20:54,590
What does it have to do with you?

361
00:20:54,590 --> 00:20:56,030
I didn't say anything.

362
00:20:56,830 --> 00:20:57,640
You're here?

363
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:58,440
Who are you?

364
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:02,160
He... he took the ball!

365
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:06,350
Thief! Thief!

366
00:21:06,350 --> 00:21:07,000
Stop him!

367
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,200
Stop right there!

368
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:12,160
Stop right there!

369
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:17,630
[Accessible Route]

370
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:16,440
Don't move! What did you take?

371
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:17,100
Let go of me!

372
00:21:18,310 --> 00:21:19,400
I saw it! Honey!

373
00:21:19,400 --> 00:21:19,960
Here comes another one!

374
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:20,640
Here!

375
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:21,960
Pry his hands open! Pry his hands open!

376
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:22,480
Listen to me!

377
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:23,440
Pry his hands open!

378
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:24,110
Give it to me!

379
00:21:24,110 --> 00:21:25,170
Pry his hands open!

380
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:26,480
Take it! Take it!

381
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:27,200
Give it back to me!

382
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:27,720
It's mine!

383
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:28,200
Give it to me!

384
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:28,800
It's mine!

385
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:30,000
What?

386
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:32,000
What are you doing?

387
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:32,680
Doctor!

388
00:21:32,250 --> 00:21:36,560
[Accessible Route]

389
00:21:32,830 --> 00:21:33,790
Call the police, Doctor!

390
00:21:33,790 --> 00:21:34,440
What's going on?

391
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:35,310
There's a thief!

392
00:21:35,310 --> 00:21:35,920
Wait a minute.

393
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:36,790
No, no, no!

394
00:21:36,790 --> 00:21:38,440
-No! Don't call the police!
-You stole our stuff!

395
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,770
Now you're scared, huh?

396
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:41,960
Comrade.

397
00:21:42,310 --> 00:21:43,570
You hit me pretty hard.

398
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:44,960
This shows

399
00:21:45,550 --> 00:21:47,550
your loyalty to the revolution.

400
00:21:47,960 --> 00:21:48,750
Comrade!

401
00:21:49,440 --> 00:21:50,700
We are on the same side.

402
00:21:51,110 --> 00:21:52,510
You don't know anything.

403
00:21:52,510 --> 00:21:53,570
What should I know?

404
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:54,680
This contains

405
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:56,000
important intelligence

406
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:57,240
related to national security!

407
00:21:57,240 --> 00:21:59,270
I need to take it to Beijing

408
00:21:59,310 --> 00:22:00,830
and hand it to my chief personally,

409
00:22:00,830 --> 00:22:01,480
Zhang...

410
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:03,350
I can't tell you

411
00:22:03,350 --> 00:22:04,270
who my chief is.

412
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:05,750
Dawn is just around the corner!

413
00:22:05,750 --> 00:22:07,080
Just around the corner!

414
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:10,140
I studied medicine because of my family.

415
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:12,080
I was young and ignorant.

416
00:22:12,750 --> 00:22:15,310
I thought being a doctor
would make me a lot of money.

417
00:22:15,310 --> 00:22:17,640
I didn't expect that it would take
8 years just to graduate.

418
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:19,030
Even so, after graduation,

419
00:22:19,030 --> 00:22:19,550
I had no choice

420
00:22:19,550 --> 00:22:20,920
but to work here.

421
00:22:21,350 --> 00:22:23,150
Do you think it was my own choice?

422
00:22:23,750 --> 00:22:25,680
The base salary is just over 3,000.

423
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:27,200
Adding everything up,

424
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:28,130
it's only 5,000.

425
00:22:28,350 --> 00:22:29,480
What can I do with it?

426
00:22:30,110 --> 00:22:31,680
Even so, many patients still think

427
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:32,790
that we are to blame for the difficulty

428
00:22:32,790 --> 00:22:34,440
and high cost of seeing a doctor.

429
00:22:34,440 --> 00:22:35,590
What can I do?

430
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:37,680
The overall environment is just like this.

431
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:38,510
And I don't have your luck.

432
00:22:38,510 --> 00:22:39,640
I can't get out.

433
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:43,320
I just want to rely on myself.

434
00:22:44,240 --> 00:22:45,030
I'm improving myself,

435
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:45,750
applying for a PhD,

436
00:22:45,750 --> 00:22:47,240
and taking professional title exams,

437
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:48,550
so that I can make more money

438
00:22:48,550 --> 00:22:49,240
and improve

439
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:50,030
my family's quality of life.

440
00:22:50,030 --> 00:22:51,960
Is there anything wrong with that?

441
00:22:54,030 --> 00:22:55,400
There's nothing wrong with that.

442
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:56,110
Don't get worked up.

443
00:22:56,110 --> 00:22:57,110
I'm not worked up.

444
00:22:57,310 --> 00:22:58,680
Why would I be worked up?

445
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:02,350
You... You said I'm sleepy during the day

446
00:23:02,350 --> 00:23:03,480
and slack off at night.

447
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:04,200
That's because...

448
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:04,880
Mingming!

449
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:05,640
What?

450
00:23:05,940 --> 00:23:09,160
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

451
00:23:06,110 --> 00:23:07,440
Your... your dad's...

452
00:23:13,590 --> 00:23:15,030
He usually forgets about it afterwards.

453
00:23:15,030 --> 00:23:16,830
I didn't expect him to remember it
this time.

454
00:23:16,830 --> 00:23:17,830
I'm really sorry

455
00:23:17,830 --> 00:23:19,030
for causing you trouble.

456
00:23:19,030 --> 00:23:20,640
I'll definitely
keep an eye on him from now on.

457
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:21,440
It's fine.

458
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:22,830
Well, if you need anything,
just let me know.

459
00:23:22,830 --> 00:23:24,030
I'll head back first.

460
00:23:25,750 --> 00:23:26,400
Stop looking!

461
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:27,110
Move along! Move along!

462
00:23:27,110 --> 00:23:27,750
There's nothing to see.

463
00:23:27,750 --> 00:23:28,310
Go now.

464
00:23:28,310 --> 00:23:29,310
Mingming really

465
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:30,590
has it tough.

466
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:34,110
That guy just now

467
00:23:34,110 --> 00:23:35,160
was Mingming's father.

468
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:36,560
His name is Che Changhai.

469
00:23:36,960 --> 00:23:38,960
He has moderate schizophrenia,

470
00:23:39,270 --> 00:23:40,110
the kind that no matter how you treat it,

471
00:23:40,110 --> 00:23:41,310
it can't be cured.

472
00:23:42,590 --> 00:23:44,680
He... He firmly believes

473
00:23:44,680 --> 00:23:45,680
that he is

474
00:23:45,830 --> 00:23:47,310
here to protect national security

475
00:23:47,310 --> 00:23:49,970
and is an undercover agent
for an organization.

476
00:23:59,270 --> 00:24:00,200
Comrade Xiaobo.

477
00:24:02,110 --> 00:24:04,510
I've encountered many difficulties here.

478
00:24:04,830 --> 00:24:06,030
Please continue.

479
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:06,960
He said

480
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:09,510
that after completing his mission,

481
00:24:09,510 --> 00:24:10,880
he would return to Beijing

482
00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:12,350
and go to a secret base

483
00:24:12,510 --> 00:24:13,480
to work.

484
00:24:13,790 --> 00:24:14,750
Could what he said

485
00:24:14,750 --> 00:24:16,230
be true?

486
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:20,310
Mingming, this girl,

487
00:24:20,310 --> 00:24:21,070
is a

488
00:24:21,070 --> 00:24:22,400
very proud person.

489
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:24,350
When she was in elementary school,

490
00:24:24,350 --> 00:24:25,510
her dad got sick.

491
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:27,160
Then, he kept

492
00:24:27,160 --> 00:24:28,360
causing her trouble.

493
00:24:28,750 --> 00:24:30,160
You see, from her college years

494
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:31,270
to her working life,

495
00:24:31,270 --> 00:24:32,790
her dad has always been

496
00:24:33,310 --> 00:24:34,590
a burden on her

497
00:24:35,270 --> 00:24:36,400
in her daily life.

498
00:24:37,310 --> 00:24:38,910
That's really tough for her.

499
00:24:39,510 --> 00:24:41,200
Sometimes I think

500
00:24:41,270 --> 00:24:42,640
she and Zhang Hao got a divorce

501
00:24:42,640 --> 00:24:44,030
because of

502
00:24:44,030 --> 00:24:45,030
her family situation.

503
00:24:45,030 --> 00:24:46,440
She was married?

504
00:24:47,270 --> 00:24:48,440
Who is Zhang Hao?

505
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:51,200
He's the guy sitting over there.

506
00:24:59,260 --> 00:25:00,260
[No Unauthorized Entry
into Doctors' Lounge]

507
00:25:08,160 --> 00:25:09,790
I wasn't finished speaking earlier.

508
00:25:09,790 --> 00:25:11,110
Didn't you say I'm sleepy during the day

509
00:25:11,110 --> 00:25:12,000
and slack off at night,

510
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:13,830
and that I don't really want to take
the PhD exam?

511
00:25:13,830 --> 00:25:15,350
If you have time, come with me.

512
00:25:15,350 --> 00:25:16,070
I'll take you to see

513
00:25:16,070 --> 00:25:17,400
where I work part-time.

514
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:19,920
Can I go?

515
00:25:22,160 --> 00:25:23,160
Bring me along.

516
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:46,720
Hello?

517
00:25:48,160 --> 00:25:49,820
Do you have a solo photo of Mom?

518
00:25:53,720 --> 00:25:54,510
No.

519
00:25:58,750 --> 00:25:59,790
Right, I don't even have one.

520
00:25:59,790 --> 00:26:00,680
How could you?

521
00:26:02,110 --> 00:26:03,440
I shouldn't have asked.

522
00:26:15,270 --> 00:26:16,070
What's wrong?

523
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:21,680
We're here.

524
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:26,890
[Fucheng Transport Company]

525
00:26:27,940 --> 00:26:33,120
[Fucheng City Taxi]

526
00:26:47,390 --> 00:26:52,410
[Little Pepper Stage: Blossoming Passion]

527
00:26:52,540 --> 00:26:58,140
[Little Pepper Stage]

528
00:27:00,200 --> 00:27:01,000
I really didn't expect

529
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:03,240
the theater for the sing-and-dance duet

530
00:27:03,240 --> 00:27:04,110
to be like this now.

531
00:27:04,110 --> 00:27:07,160
It's my first time watching
a sing-and-dance duet here.

532
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:08,310
How is that possible?

533
00:27:08,310 --> 00:27:09,960
You've lived in the Northeast
for so many years.

534
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:10,440
No.

535
00:27:10,790 --> 00:27:11,960
I've seen sing-and-dance duets before,

536
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:13,480
but this is my first time
seeing one in a theater.

537
00:27:13,480 --> 00:27:14,510
I used to think

538
00:27:14,510 --> 00:27:15,480
that the people who came to the theater

539
00:27:15,480 --> 00:27:16,920
were all elders.

540
00:27:17,240 --> 00:27:18,480
I just realized after coming here

541
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:20,480
that there are so many young people.

542
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:34,270
Listen up, you two.

543
00:27:34,350 --> 00:27:35,750
You two will open the show today

544
00:27:35,750 --> 00:27:38,680
and sing the new version
of "Widow Ma Running a Shop."

545
00:27:39,070 --> 00:27:39,750
Mr. Wang.

546
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:41,490
Mr. Wang, wait a minute.

547
00:27:42,880 --> 00:27:44,750
Didn't I just tell you?

548
00:27:44,750 --> 00:27:46,350
I have two colleagues here today.

549
00:27:46,350 --> 00:27:47,440
I don't want to sing dirty songs.

550
00:27:47,440 --> 00:27:49,270
Come on. You sing clean songs every day,

551
00:27:49,270 --> 00:27:50,160
and that has driven away several

552
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:50,790
of my regular customers.

553
00:27:50,790 --> 00:27:51,960
Don't you know that?

554
00:27:52,160 --> 00:27:52,920
If you don't sing,

555
00:27:52,920 --> 00:27:54,000
get out of here today.

556
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:55,530
Don't be a dog in the manger!

557
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:56,830
You two, sing dirty songs.

558
00:27:56,830 --> 00:27:57,920
You all have to sing dirty songs today!

559
00:27:57,920 --> 00:27:58,270
Okay.

560
00:27:58,270 --> 00:27:58,680
Okay.

561
00:28:10,440 --> 00:28:13,310
Sis, you can't do anything
about Manager Wang.

562
00:28:14,030 --> 00:28:15,440
We're just trying to make a living.

563
00:28:15,440 --> 00:28:17,570
There's no shame in singing anything.

564
00:28:20,510 --> 00:28:21,370
Little Jujube.

565
00:28:22,750 --> 00:28:24,750
We've been partners for half a year.

566
00:28:24,920 --> 00:28:26,400
You know my temper.

567
00:28:27,960 --> 00:28:29,690
I can't get along with that guy.

568
00:28:32,750 --> 00:28:33,960
Today might be my last time

569
00:28:33,960 --> 00:28:35,160
performing here.

570
00:28:35,750 --> 00:28:37,030
Can you do me a favor?

571
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:39,790
Sure.

572
00:28:40,240 --> 00:28:41,480
I've always found that guy Wang

573
00:28:41,480 --> 00:28:42,400
annoying.

574
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:43,750
I'll help you beat him up.

575
00:28:43,750 --> 00:28:45,410
Wait here. I'll go find a sack.

576
00:28:45,830 --> 00:28:47,110
That's not what I meant.

577
00:28:47,110 --> 00:28:48,310
Then what do you mean?

578
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:06,400
Bravo! Bravo! Bravo!

579
00:29:04,450 --> 00:29:07,590
[Little Pepper Stage]

580
00:29:09,920 --> 00:29:10,960
Not bad. Not bad.

581
00:29:14,790 --> 00:29:16,510
Thank you all

582
00:29:16,510 --> 00:29:19,070
for coming to Little Pepper Stage.

583
00:29:19,240 --> 00:29:21,110
I'm your host, Wang Tiezhu.

584
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:22,640
I'm your host, Lin Lin.

585
00:29:22,960 --> 00:29:24,480
You're all regular customers,

586
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:25,810
so without further ado,

587
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:28,310
let's welcome our most fabulous duo,

588
00:29:28,350 --> 00:29:29,270
Little Jujube!

589
00:29:29,270 --> 00:29:30,350
And Big Pomegranate,

590
00:29:30,350 --> 00:29:32,510
to bring you the opening performance,

591
00:29:32,510 --> 00:29:34,590
"Widow Ma Running a Shop!"

592
00:29:34,590 --> 00:29:37,120
Please welcome them
with a round of applause!

593
00:29:48,640 --> 00:29:50,270
My dear folks,

594
00:29:50,270 --> 00:29:52,310
good evening!

595
00:29:52,480 --> 00:29:53,270
Bravo!

596
00:29:53,350 --> 00:29:56,510
Bravo! Bravo!

597
00:29:56,750 --> 00:29:58,590
I am Big Pomegranate!

598
00:29:56,980 --> 00:30:00,340
[Widow Ma Running a Shop]

599
00:29:58,590 --> 00:30:01,070
I am your favorite Little Jujube!

600
00:30:02,110 --> 00:30:03,910
The applause isn't loud enough.

601
00:30:05,640 --> 00:30:07,350
Thank you all for coming.

602
00:30:11,780 --> 00:30:21,650
[Widow Ma Running a Shop]
[Big Pomegranate & Little Jujube]

603
00:30:13,310 --> 00:30:17,550
♪ I fall to my knees and kowtow ♪

604
00:30:17,550 --> 00:30:20,960
♪ Tears streaming down my face ♪

605
00:30:19,680 --> 00:30:21,480
Shouldn't this be about a widow?

606
00:30:22,200 --> 00:30:23,110
♪ Zhonghua ♪

607
00:30:23,110 --> 00:30:24,960
♪ Godmother ♪

608
00:30:24,960 --> 00:30:26,960
An empress dowager is also a widow.

609
00:30:27,070 --> 00:30:27,920
Is that so?

610
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:29,640
I think they made a mistake.

611
00:30:29,640 --> 00:30:32,400
Isn't this
"Bao Zhen Judging the Empress Dowager?"

612
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:33,790
Wh-Who let them sing this?

613
00:30:33,790 --> 00:30:34,680
I don't know.

614
00:30:34,680 --> 00:30:35,680
What is this?

615
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:44,550
♪ Godmother ♪

616
00:30:44,640 --> 00:30:46,070
♪ Zhonghua ♪

617
00:30:46,070 --> 00:30:47,350
♪ Godmother ♪

618
00:30:55,310 --> 00:31:02,680
♪ You are so kind and filial ♪

619
00:31:02,960 --> 00:31:09,920
♪ I can't bear to leave you behind ♪

620
00:31:10,880 --> 00:31:14,030
♪ All these years ♪

621
00:31:14,680 --> 00:31:18,480
♪ You've been running around for me ♪

622
00:31:18,550 --> 00:31:22,530
♪ Begging on the streets ♪

623
00:31:22,750 --> 00:31:26,200
♪ You've suffered a lot ♪

624
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:29,960
♪ For me ♪

625
00:31:30,160 --> 00:31:33,000
♪ Without you ♪

626
00:31:33,240 --> 00:31:37,500
♪ I wouldn't still be alive ♪

627
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:40,750
♪ Without you, I couldn't have ♪

628
00:31:40,750 --> 00:31:44,480
♪ Gotten my revenge ♪

629
00:32:22,740 --> 00:32:26,590
[Notice]

630
00:32:28,720 --> 00:32:30,110
Your baby has been born.

631
00:32:30,110 --> 00:32:31,370
Take a look at the baby.

632
00:32:31,480 --> 00:32:33,110
The baby was born

633
00:32:33,110 --> 00:32:34,240
at 10:08,

634
00:32:34,240 --> 00:32:35,750
weighing 3,200 grams.

635
00:32:35,880 --> 00:32:36,790
It's a boy.

636
00:32:36,790 --> 00:32:38,320
All indicators are normal.

637
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:40,350
He'll go back to the ward with you later.

638
00:32:40,350 --> 00:32:41,480
You can hold him now.

639
00:33:18,030 --> 00:33:21,270
I wouldn't still be alive.

640
00:33:21,960 --> 00:33:25,000
Without you, I couldn't have

641
00:33:25,070 --> 00:33:29,270
gotten my revenge.

642
00:33:35,350 --> 00:33:36,080
Zhengliang?

643
00:33:36,440 --> 00:33:37,400
What's wrong, Zhengliang?

644
00:33:37,400 --> 00:33:38,930
Didn't they come together?

645
00:34:37,150 --> 00:34:40,790
[With Deepest Sympathy]

646
00:34:37,230 --> 00:34:41,510
Please bow to Ms. Li Zhongling

647
00:34:40,850 --> 00:34:46,610
[Ever-Present Voice and Countenance]

648
00:34:42,590 --> 00:34:43,840
three times.

649
00:34:46,880 --> 00:34:47,960
First bow.

650
00:34:55,190 --> 00:34:56,280
Second bow.

651
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:02,070
Third bow.

652
00:35:08,030 --> 00:35:10,880
Please pay your respects to the deceased

653
00:35:11,190 --> 00:35:13,520
and offer your condolences to the family.

654
00:35:18,570 --> 00:35:21,820
[In Memoriam]

655
00:35:38,070 --> 00:35:39,000
My condolences.

656
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:42,810
My condolences.

657
00:35:45,380 --> 00:35:48,500
♪ A soul that came to earth
amid the cries ♪

658
00:35:48,920 --> 00:35:52,090
♪ Welcome to this city of haste ♪

659
00:35:52,560 --> 00:35:54,750
♪ Grow taller, quick as you can ♪

660
00:35:54,670 --> 00:35:55,320
My condolences.

661
00:35:55,160 --> 00:35:57,510
♪ Learn how to find your footing ♪

662
00:35:59,750 --> 00:36:03,020
♪ A soul who hid
among the lanes and alleys ♪

663
00:36:03,500 --> 00:36:06,720
♪ A single turn, and the lamp
at the door grows distant ♪

664
00:36:05,360 --> 00:36:08,070
Bid a final farewell to your mother.

665
00:36:07,160 --> 00:36:09,400
♪ The ticket bears no way back ♪

666
00:36:08,250 --> 00:36:12,430
[A Virtuous Mother for All Ages]

667
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:12,180
♪ How like life it is ♪

668
00:36:12,760 --> 00:36:13,560
First kowtow.

669
00:36:14,350 --> 00:36:17,650
♪ One who nestled close
on a winter's night ♪

670
00:36:18,010 --> 00:36:21,200
♪ A bite of food beside a pool of gaze ♪

671
00:36:21,760 --> 00:36:24,000
♪ When summer dusk arrives ♪

672
00:36:22,230 --> 00:36:24,630
Mother's soul returns to heaven.

673
00:36:24,420 --> 00:36:26,370
♪ We'll go to see the flowers ♪

674
00:36:25,190 --> 00:36:26,360
Second kowtow.

675
00:36:28,940 --> 00:36:32,170
♪ One who was stranded on the road ♪

676
00:36:31,320 --> 00:36:33,400
Bless the family with peace.

677
00:36:32,590 --> 00:36:35,720
♪ Heels buried under unseen snow ♪

678
00:36:33,960 --> 00:36:35,030
Third kowtow.

679
00:36:36,200 --> 00:36:38,440
♪ Don't panic—the journey is long ♪

680
00:36:37,920 --> 00:36:40,030
Pray for blessings upon the world.

681
00:36:38,810 --> 00:36:41,330
♪ Long enough to hold your pause ♪

682
00:36:43,840 --> 00:36:45,000
In this world,

683
00:36:45,840 --> 00:36:48,510
the kindness that can never be repaid

684
00:36:49,280 --> 00:36:51,800
is a mother's love and care.

685
00:36:55,190 --> 00:37:01,190
Mother is leaving today,

686
00:37:01,710 --> 00:37:07,590
and my heart truly aches.

687
00:37:09,110 --> 00:37:15,230
Tears fill my eyes.

688
00:37:16,620 --> 00:37:19,910
♪ You'll pass through the seasons,
through dawn and dusk ♪

689
00:37:20,350 --> 00:37:23,500
♪ Hearing someone call your name,
again and again ♪

690
00:37:23,950 --> 00:37:26,210
♪ These ties may hurt a little ♪

691
00:37:26,710 --> 00:37:28,910
♪ Don't heal a broken heart ♪

692
00:37:31,180 --> 00:37:34,290
♪ It will bear witness
to the life you bravely lived ♪

693
00:37:34,900 --> 00:37:38,060
♪ To the beautiful souls you've loved ♪

694
00:37:38,560 --> 00:37:40,730
♪ To the address you call home ♪

695
00:37:41,240 --> 00:37:43,920
♪ In the little town
you've wandered through ♪

696
00:37:46,410 --> 00:37:48,780
♪ The wind in the city ♪

697
00:37:49,160 --> 00:37:51,910
♪ Blows through dreams
that flicker between light and dark ♪

698
00:37:52,980 --> 00:37:55,590
♪ Blows through one soul's radiance ♪

699
00:37:57,150 --> 00:37:59,360
♪ And all its weathered scars ♪

700
00:38:01,150 --> 00:38:03,300
♪ Blows through the depths of winter ♪

701
00:38:03,680 --> 00:38:06,480
♪ Stumbling along in the wind ♪

702
00:38:07,590 --> 00:38:10,160
♪ Flickering along in the wind ♪

703
00:38:11,740 --> 00:38:17,580
♪ Toward the crossroads
brimming with sunlight ♪

704
00:38:21,260 --> 00:38:24,430
♪ May every road you take be safe ♪

705
00:38:24,640 --> 00:38:28,790
♪ May the scenery stay simple
and carry you past regret ♪

706
00:38:29,250 --> 00:38:32,290
♪ Love deeply whatever comes to meet you ♪

707
00:38:32,820 --> 00:38:35,760
♪ And let those who leave be buried
under snow on the hills ♪

708
00:38:36,530 --> 00:38:38,950
♪ May you come home covered in dust ♪

709
00:38:39,280 --> 00:38:43,160
♪ Held by what you love
as you roam the world and return ♪

710
00:38:39,950 --> 00:38:45,240
[Xiaoximen Hospital,
Helping You Live a Healthier Life]

711
00:38:44,310 --> 00:38:48,710
♪ Saying she was so beautiful
in front of the door ♪

712
00:38:47,090 --> 00:38:53,170
[Funeral Wreaths and Burial Clothing]

713
00:38:47,150 --> 00:38:48,550
That lady was quite a decent person.

714
00:38:48,550 --> 00:38:49,510
Too decent.

715
00:38:49,550 --> 00:38:50,960
The pay is good, huh?

716
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:52,550
What should we eat tonight?

717
00:38:52,550 --> 00:38:53,400
Barbecue.

718
00:38:57,150 --> 00:38:58,080
Eat more shrimp.

719
00:39:04,280 --> 00:39:05,120
Ch-Chen.

720
00:39:05,440 --> 00:39:06,040
What's up?

721
00:39:06,800 --> 00:39:08,200
Can I tell you something?

722
00:39:08,280 --> 00:39:09,070
Go ahead.

723
00:39:10,550 --> 00:39:11,440
This month,

724
00:39:11,550 --> 00:39:13,210
after I help you open the shop,

725
00:39:13,510 --> 00:39:14,400
I'll quit.

726
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:18,740
What do you mean?
What are you going to do?

727
00:39:21,150 --> 00:39:22,960
I'm thinking of going
to Beijing to try my luck.

728
00:39:22,960 --> 00:39:24,360
You're going to Beijing?

729
00:39:32,800 --> 00:39:34,150
Do you know anyone in Beijing

730
00:39:34,150 --> 00:39:34,840
or what?

731
00:39:34,960 --> 00:39:36,490
Did someone offer you a job?

732
00:39:37,150 --> 00:39:39,480
Wh-Where are you going to live over there?

733
00:39:41,480 --> 00:39:42,840
I haven't thought about it yet.

734
00:39:42,840 --> 00:39:43,590
But it's fine.

735
00:39:43,590 --> 00:39:43,960
For this kind of thing,

736
00:39:43,960 --> 00:39:45,230
I'll just take it one step at a time.

737
00:39:45,230 --> 00:39:47,160
I won't starve to death in this era.

738
00:39:47,670 --> 00:39:48,440
It's mainly because I really can't

739
00:39:48,440 --> 00:39:50,100
keep staying at home anymore.

740
00:39:50,590 --> 00:39:51,360
Now whatever I see

741
00:39:51,360 --> 00:39:52,490
reminds me of my mom.

742
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:53,800
It's too painful.

743
00:39:57,480 --> 00:39:59,540
Did you discuss it with your brother?

744
00:40:01,030 --> 00:40:02,760
What's there to discuss with him?

745
00:40:02,760 --> 00:40:03,550
You two are brothers.

746
00:40:03,550 --> 00:40:05,480
Shouldn't you discuss it with him?

747
00:40:07,150 --> 00:40:08,070
Isn't he the closest person

748
00:40:08,070 --> 00:40:09,530
you have in this world now?

749
00:40:09,630 --> 00:40:10,710
He's been in a big city

750
00:40:10,710 --> 00:40:12,400
for so many years. He has experience.

751
00:40:12,400 --> 00:40:13,930
Chen, let me put it this way.

752
00:40:14,230 --> 00:40:15,840
He's just a family member of mine

753
00:40:15,840 --> 00:40:17,800
who happens to share some blood with me.

754
00:40:17,800 --> 00:40:19,030
We're not close at all.

755
00:40:19,030 --> 00:40:20,630
Why are you acting like this?

756
00:40:21,400 --> 00:40:22,730
Are you still mad at him?

757
00:40:25,880 --> 00:40:27,590
Didn't he attend the funeral?

758
00:40:28,360 --> 00:40:29,960
Chen, the goods are here.

759
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:30,480
Okay, okay.

760
00:40:30,480 --> 00:40:31,080
I'll do it.

761
00:40:31,630 --> 00:40:32,890
Give them to me, buddy.

762
00:40:35,800 --> 00:40:36,840
You can just leave the rest here.

763
00:40:36,840 --> 00:40:37,110
Alright.

764
00:40:37,110 --> 00:40:37,570
Thanks.

765
00:40:39,190 --> 00:40:41,030
Your expectations of him are too low.

766
00:40:41,030 --> 00:40:42,290
I'm warning you, Chen.

767
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:43,150
Don't let his

768
00:40:43,150 --> 00:40:44,360
halo of an excellent surgeon

769
00:40:44,360 --> 00:40:45,230
deceive you.

770
00:40:45,510 --> 00:40:46,400
This guy

771
00:40:46,400 --> 00:40:47,360
is heartless and ungrateful,

772
00:40:47,360 --> 00:40:48,110
and definitely not a good match.

773
00:40:48,110 --> 00:40:50,230
Well, you also admit he's excellent,

774
00:40:50,230 --> 00:40:50,880
right?

775
00:40:51,150 --> 00:40:53,280
What's the use of him being excellent?

776
00:40:53,590 --> 00:40:55,250
It's all for outsiders to see.

777
00:40:55,590 --> 00:40:58,110
Anyone in his family
is bound to have bad luck.

778
00:40:58,110 --> 00:40:59,360
Since he came back,

779
00:40:59,360 --> 00:41:01,090
he hasn't cared about me at all.

780
00:41:04,840 --> 00:41:06,900
Maybe you just don't know that he has.

781
00:41:10,440 --> 00:41:12,000
Chen, the goods are all here.

782
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:12,670
Thanks, buddy.

783
00:41:12,670 --> 00:41:13,150
Okay.

784
00:41:13,150 --> 00:41:13,880
Just pile them here.

785
00:41:13,880 --> 00:41:14,880
Alright. I'm leaving, Chen.

786
00:41:14,880 --> 00:41:15,360
Bye.

787
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:15,960
Bye.

788
00:41:22,070 --> 00:41:22,760
Dr. Liu!

789
00:41:23,360 --> 00:41:24,070
Dr. Liu!

790
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:25,760
There's a patient in the ER

791
00:41:25,760 --> 00:41:27,090
with an open head injury

792
00:41:27,230 --> 00:41:28,430
that we can't handle!

793
00:41:29,760 --> 00:41:30,550
Coming.

794
00:41:54,250 --> 00:41:58,930
[Entrance] [Stroke Fast Track]

795
00:41:59,520 --> 00:42:01,800
[No Entry]

796
00:42:04,230 --> 00:42:05,030
Dr. Liu.

797
00:42:05,150 --> 00:42:06,030
Blood pressure 150 over 90.

798
00:42:06,030 --> 00:42:06,890
Heart rate 110.

799
00:42:08,760 --> 00:42:09,280
Ma'am.

800
00:42:10,070 --> 00:42:10,880
Ma'am.

801
00:42:14,710 --> 00:42:16,110
Do you know where you are?

802
00:42:16,800 --> 00:42:17,960
I don't know.

803
00:42:19,760 --> 00:42:20,890
How did you get hurt?

804
00:42:22,440 --> 00:42:24,280
Hit by a bat.

805
00:42:24,590 --> 00:42:26,120
I heard her husband hit her.

806
00:42:27,760 --> 00:42:28,760
The CT scan is out.

807
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:30,200
Let me see the wounds.

808
00:42:36,480 --> 00:42:37,840
Is Director Tong in the hospital today?

809
00:42:37,840 --> 00:42:39,960
No, he went to the provincial capital
for a meeting.

810
00:42:39,960 --> 00:42:40,760
Prepare an operating room.

811
00:42:40,760 --> 00:42:42,320
Yang Ran, you'll be my first assistant.

812
00:42:42,320 --> 00:42:42,960
Who? Me?

813
00:42:43,710 --> 00:42:44,880
I don't have any...

814
00:42:44,880 --> 00:42:46,880
experience
handling this kind of situation.

815
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:49,140
I'll schedule an operating room for you.

816
00:42:51,960 --> 00:42:52,510
You do it.

817
00:42:54,280 --> 00:42:55,000
I can't.

818
00:42:56,110 --> 00:42:58,710
I haven't been in an operating room
for 2 years.

819
00:43:04,230 --> 00:43:05,360
Call Che Mingming.

820
00:43:06,150 --> 00:43:07,070
Tell her to come over immediately.
